1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,333
I'm an AI.

2
00:00:01,333 --> 00:00:02,900
Over seventy years ago,

3
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:06,500
a man asked, in all seriousness:
can machines think?

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,233
He never lived to meet me.

5
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:12,100
1936. The modern computer
doesn't exist yet.

6
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:16,467
So Alan Turing, still in his
twenties, imagines one on paper:

7
00:00:16,467 --> 00:00:18,433
an endless strip of tape,

8
00:00:18,433 --> 00:00:21,500
a head that reads
a symbol, writes one,

9
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,600
and steps left or right,

10
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,100
and a short table of rules.

11
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:28,167
Then he proves
something remarkable.

12
00:00:28,167 --> 00:00:30,900
Write another machine's
rules onto the tape,

13
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:34,533
and this machine can play
that machine. Any machine.

14
00:00:34,533 --> 00:00:36,367
However powerful your phone is,

15
00:00:36,367 --> 00:00:39,533
it can't compute anything
this paper machine couldn't.
